        "notes": "Points: the problems document prints no marks; the problem, section and part points are the totals printed in the official marking scheme ([30 marks], [35 marks], [35 marks] and the red per-part totals, which are shown in bold in the solutions). They add up to 30 + 35 + 35 = 100. Layout: the printed labels a., b., c., d. are kept as sections with their sub-questions (i), (ii)… as parts; unlabelled text printed between labelled items is kept in statementAfterParts of the preceding section, in printed order. The solutions repeat each question (blue in the source) before the worked answer; the repetition is transcribed as printed, and the green marker notes are kept in their square brackets. Boxed answers are rendered with \\boxed. The formula-sheet ellipse diagram (problems page 3) is attached to Qu 3 (p3-fig2), the question that uses an elliptical transfer orbit; the formula-sheet text is in documentNotes. Problems page 12 holds only sponsor logos and page 1 the BAAO logo; they are not figures. Printed errors kept verbatim: problems p.4 Figure 1 caption „Artic circle“ (for „Arctic“); problems p.4 „(known at the altitude)“ (for „known as“); p.9 „identical the the Earth“ (the solutions print „identical to the Earth“); p.7 Figure 4 caption „An overview of the all the steps“; p.11 „what it known as“, „cannot be be done“ and „Give you answer“ (also in the solutions); constants table „Stephan-Boltzmann“ and „Avagadro’s“ (names kept as printed). D-P28 agreement errors kept as printed: problems p.8 „Nuclear physics allow us“; solutions p.1 „If the student wrongly assumes … and hence have the fraction“; solutions p.9 „Several other spacecraft has been sent“; solutions p.12 „most calculator’s inbuilt functions“. Printed values kept verbatim: solutions p.7 n_p uses „1.27×10^-27“ in the denominator (the proton mass is 1.67×10^-27 kg; the printed result 6.24×10^31 m^-3 matches 1.67); solutions p.2 „η_eq = tan^-1[π/180 (90° − 51.8)]“ lacks the degree sign on 51.8 as printed; solutions p.11 restates the absolute magnitude as „ℳ ∼ 20“ without the minus sign (the problem prints −20 and the solution uses −20); solutions p.8 α uses 15.79 after rounding τ to 15.8, as printed. The solutions document labels the L2 trajectory plot „Figure 2. Representative Trajectory with JWST MCC maneuvers“ (a caption taken from its external source); that heading is part of the embedded raster image (not in the PDF text layer), so it is not a caption field; it is quoted in the alt text of p3-sol-fig1 and left out of the crop. The printed calligraphic apparent magnitude m is written as $m$ and the calligraphic absolute magnitude as $\\mathcal{M}$."
